# Semantic xref lane 1

Source SHA-256: `HASH`

Review every note cross-reference semantically, not merely numerically. Compare the source claim and source note with the target note and its accompanying body text. Follow short Id. chains using the included target neighborhood. Report a high-impact xref finding when the target exists but does not support the source call site; turn genuine ambiguity into an author query.
Return `lane-results/xref_semantic_001.json` with lane `xref_semantic_001` using the lane-result schema.

```json
[
  {
    "source_block_id": "FN1",
    "source_display_number": 1,
    "source_text": "See supra note 1.",
    "source_call_sites": [
      {
        "block_id": "B000001",
        "heading_path": [],
        "text": "The court found that that rule applies."
      }
    ],
    "reference": {
      "direction": null,
      "label": null,
      "char_start": null,
      "char_end": null,
      "excerpt": null
    },
    "target_block_id": "FN1",
    "target_display_number": 1,
    "target_text": "See supra note 1.",
    "target_call_sites": [
      {
        "block_id": "B000001",
        "heading_path": [],
        "text": "The court found that that rule applies."
      }
    ],
    "target_neighborhood": [
      {
        "block_id": "FN1",
        "display_number": 1,
        "text": "See supra note 1."
      }
    ]
  }
]
```
